# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit a real `.env`.
#
# `pnpm --filter @vuarau/api ops:check-env` judges a filled-in copy and prints no
# value it read. The full contract is docs/11-operations/deployment-contract.md.

# development (a laptop, the end-to-end suite) or pilot (a real depot).
# `pilot` refuses HS256, and requires https for the issuer and the public origin.
APP_ENV=development

# The https origin a phone actually opens. Required when APP_ENV=pilot.
# PUBLIC_APP_ORIGIN=https://pilot.example.vn

# Postgres connection used by migrations, seeds, and the `db` test project.
# When unset, `pnpm test:db` skips its suites instead of failing.
#
# Local Docker container created during bootstrap:
#   docker run -d --name vuarau-ops-dev-pg \
#     -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres -e POSTGRES_USER=postgres -e POSTGRES_DB=vuarau_test \
#     -p 55432:5432 postgres:17-alpine
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:55432/vuarau_test

# --- Supabase authentication (Milestone 1) -----------------------------------
# The API verifies bearer tokens and resolves `sub` to a local actor. Without
# these the server refuses to start; tests do not need them.
SUPABASE_JWT_ISSUER=https://your-project.supabase.co/auth/v1
SUPABASE_JWT_AUDIENCE=authenticated

# Set exactly ONE of the following.
# Preferred, and the only one a pilot accepts — asymmetric keys, so this server
# never holds material that can mint a token:
# SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
# Shared secret (HS256). Development and Playwright only; REFUSED when
# APP_ENV=pilot. Treat as a credential; never commit a real value:
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# --- Supabase, in the browser (Milestone 5.5) --------------------------------
# The sign-in screen uses the official Supabase browser client. Both values are
# public by design: the URL identifies the project, and the anon key is a
# publishable key that authorises nothing on its own.
#
# The JWT *signing* material above is a credential and belongs only in the API
# process. Never put it in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable — that is a bundle a phone
# downloads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# Supabase renamed anon → publishable in 2025. Both names are read; prefer this one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=            # legacy spelling, still accepted

# Server-side copy, for `ops:check-supabase`. Same public value.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY (formerly the service-role key) is NOT set here, on purpose.
# This application never uses it: tokens are verified against JWKS, so nothing
# calls Supabase with privilege. It bypasses row-level security, so an unused copy
# in this file is only a chance for somebody later to reach for it.

# Where the browser's same-origin /trpc rewrite points. Defaults to :3000.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# NOT for any real deployment. Set only by apps/web/playwright.config.ts, which
# runs against a real API and database but no Supabase project. It lets the app
# read a token the test harness injected, and it is inert in a production build
# regardless (see apps/web/src/api/access-token.ts, TC-WEB-024).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_E2E_AUTH_BRIDGE=1
